# Secrets of the StreamGo services (systemd EnvironmentFile of streamgo, streamgo-livekit and streamgo-mediamtx;
# owner root, group streamgo, mode 0640). One NAME=value per line, without "export". Put a value in 'single quotes'
# when it has anything but letters, digits and + - _ . / : @ = (systemd and the shell both read it literally then).
# Never put a secret in config.toml: it is refused there.
# Every other setting can be set here too, as STREAMGO_<SECTION>_<KEY>; this file wins over config.toml.
#
# The first install appends the secret key and the credentials the three services share (bin/init-env); an upgrade
# or a reinstall never replaces them. Back this file up with the data directory: without STREAMGO_SECRET_KEY the
# stored destinations and invite links cannot be read.
# After a change: systemctl restart streamgo-livekit streamgo-mediamtx streamgo
#
# MariaDB or PostgreSQL (database.driver in config.toml; not needed for SQLite)
#STREAMGO_DATABASE_DSN=
